    "text": "<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0120_eb6fb9fa57f6.jpg\" style=\"width: 478px; height: 90px;\" /><br />Deprotonation of hydrogen labelled <math> <mn>4</mn> </math> produces a conjugate base which has more stable resonating structure and a resonance structure in which negative charge is present on the electronegative oxygen atom. Therefore, hydrogen labelled <math> <mn>4</mn> </math> is most acidic."
